  "id": "por",
  "term": "POR",
  "definition": "POR here means patient-oriented research: an approach to research that includes patients as partners and brings their perspectives into the study process. In this forensic mental health context, it is described as an emerging practice supported in principle but complicated by organizational barriers, power imbalances, and concerns about tokenism and knowledge credibility.",
